\f1\fs22 As if from a trance, Sarah returned to her body. The fifth encore culminated in a crash of notes that echoed the overture. The stage went dark. They had returned to the beginning, breathless and overjoyed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah\'92s reverie collapsed when she saw sweet Tony\'92s jaw harden and his eyes become steel. He barged past Sarah and pushed the rest of the row back on their chairs. He was off somewhere with menacing intent. She tried as best she could to keep up with him as, behind her, the Elvi who had given the divine performance began to bicker about lyric choices. A punch-up broke out. Buskers charged the stage with their instruments and portable sound systems, each eager to be first to play there.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>At first, Sarah didn\'92t recognise the sages, despite their lanky string-bean physiques and patrician Gandalf beards. It must have been the Elvi garb they were wearing instead of pyjamas. Chilo took a step forward to intercept Tony, while Solo retreated a metre, and Kleoboulos serenely kept his ground. Tony rammed Chilo in the chest and sent him sprawling over a lemonade stand. He grabbed Kleoboulos by the scruff of his jumpsuit and, finding him as light as an empty wicker basket, threw him at the cowering Solo.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Tony!\'92 Sarah rushed past him and knelt by the sprawled sages.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleoboulos rose and dusted himself off. \'91Ah, I see your qualities are as expected, young Tony.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony pointed a threatening finger. \'91Stay away from Sarah, or I\'92ll\'97\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Yes, yes,\'92 Kleoboulos said with the patience of an ancient. \'91Enough, please. I have enjoyed my sufficiency of boyish outbursts for one evening, thank you.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91You\'92re not getting Sarah pregnant, you hear?\'92 Tony demanded. \'91None of you.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah stood between Tony and the sages. \'91Tony, if you\'92ll let me\'97\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91The prophecy requires a child is born,\'92 Chilo said.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleoboulos closed his eyes and stood in embarrassed silence, until he gathered his strength and nodded. \'91Recent events are all consistent with the fruition of the prophecy.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah had heard this kind of bullshit before. \'91You\'92re referring to the recent events you have meddled with and brought to pass?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Surely you see, such is our role in facilitating prophecy,\'92 Kleoboulos said.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Sounds like a stupidly elaborate way to land a lay,\'92 Sarah countered.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Hardly elaborate,\'92 Kleoboulos said. \'91To ensure the climax of the prophecy, we make only the smallest, most systemically sensitive interventions.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I bet all three of you have very small interventions,\'92 Tony wise-cracked, and made the bent-pinky-finger gesture.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah opted for dismissive sarcasm. \'91So how will this work? Whoever draws the shortest cock gets to fuck me? Or do I get the full, three-wizard gang bang?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91We beg of you, think of larger events. There is too much at stake,\'92 Solo added.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91We must act now,\'92 Chilo said. \'91A baby must be born by Christmas.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91In the name of tax, why?\'92 Sarah asked.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91We like eggnog,\'92 Solo joked, always the one trying to lift the mood from Greek tragedy.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91And then what?\'92 Sarah asked, her taste for derision returning. \'91Where is this prophecy going anyway?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91We\'92re bringing about the end of the universe!\'92 Chilo blurted, and Kleoboulos suppressed his impulses with a long measured breath.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91What?\'92 Sarah and Tony blurted.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Surely you must admit,\'92 Solo wheedled, \'91this universe is totally taxed.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Chilo elbowed Solo back. \'91So a new, perfect one can bang right in place of the old one,\'92 he said, which earned Kleoboulos stomping on his foot.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91How will you know?\'92 Sarah laughed. \'91We\'92ll all be dead!\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleoboulos raised his eyebrows and peered absently down his nose.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91OK, I\'92m having a baby so the world can end,\'92 Sarah conceded, rolling with the lunacy of it. \'91Great. Who will she become? The Antichrist? Adolf Hitler?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Actually, we would prefer you call him Richard.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91You want to call my son Dick Hitler?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Kleoboulos\'92 erect posture wilted and his lungs deflated. \'91Well, Chilo, you landed us exactly where I said you would. I need a drink.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Allow me,\'92 Solo offered and disappeared.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The remaining four stood awkwardly, Sarah curious to see what these loons would try next, and Tony hopeful his stocks were improving in Sarah\'92s estimation. Solo returned with pints of peanut-scented cocktails and handed them around.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Be a good chap,\'92 Chilo whispered to Solo, \'91and distract the marks.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91What?\'92 Solo asked as he raised his pint, and choked on a shred of pineapple.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Well done,\'92 Chilo muttered, and stealthily slipped potions into Sarah and Tony\'92s drinks. He sighed with disappointment.
